 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Pedir con educación",
    "@en": "Ask with education"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "Para pedir con cortesía son muy útiles **I'd like…** (quisiera…) y **Can I have…?** (¿me da…?, ¿me pone…?). **I want…** es gramatical, pero suele sonar más directo; el tono y la situación también importan.",
     "@en": "To ask with courtesy are very useful **I'd like…** (I would like) and **Can I have…?** (do I give?, do I get?). **I want…** is grammatical, but it usually sounds more direct; the tone and the situation also matter."
    },
    {
     "@es": "**I'd** es la forma corta de **I would**. El camarero pregunta **Would you like…?** (¿quiere…?) o **Anything else?** (¿algo más?). Al darte las cosas dice **Here you are** (aquí tiene).",
     "@en": "**I'd** is the short form of **I would**. The waiter asks **Would you like…?** (will you?) or **Anything else?** (anything else?). When you give it to you, **Here you are** says (here it is)."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Cantidades y precio",
    "@en": "Quantities and price"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "Las bebidas se piden con su recipiente: **a cup of tea** (una taza de té), **a glass of water** (un vaso de agua), **a bottle of water** (una botella de agua).",
     "@en": "The drinks are ordered with your container: **a cup of tea** (a cup of tea), **a glass of water** (a glass of water), **a bottle of water** (a bottle of water)."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Para el precio: **How much is it?** (¿cuánto es?). La moneda británica es la libra: **£6.50** se lee «six pounds fifty».",
     "@en": "For the price: **How much is it?** (how much is it?). The British currency is the pound: **£6.50** is read «six pounds fifty»."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Al final de la comida: **Can I have the bill, please?** (¿me trae la cuenta?).",
     "@en": "At the end of the meal: **Can I have the bill, please?** (can I have the check?)."
    }
   ]
  },
